00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.090
Jaime Lannister: According to legend, a huntsman
once tracked a lion that was terrorizing its

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.920
village all the way to its den.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.800
Though armed with only a spear, the man managed
to kill both the lion and its mate, but spared

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.370
the cubs.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.360
This mercy so pleased the Old Gods that they
sent a shaft of sunlight deep into the cave,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.990
gleaming off golden walls.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:50.040
The hunter became a miner and built a ringfort
to guard his new wealth.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.440
Nobody ever asks what happened to the cubs.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.470
Maybe the gods forgot about them, and they
starved.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.780
Maybe there never were any cubs or lions or
hunter, doesn't matter.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:04.600
Someone found enough gold in that cave to
buy whatever truth he wanted, along with a

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.969
castle that he'd name after his new family.

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:10.549
Casterly Rock.

00:01:10.549 --> 00:01:15.319
Thanks to that gold, Casterly Rock soon became
the largest, wealthiest, and best-defended

00:01:15.319 --> 00:01:16.649
castle in Westeros.

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:21.009
An army that struggled up the main approach
would still have to climb thick, high, and

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:22.789
well-defended walls.

00:01:22.789 --> 00:01:27.219
Should they choose instead to lay siege, the
sea helpfully carved a massive cave beneath

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:33.070
the castle, which over time, became a private
port complete with docks, wharves, and shipyards.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:39.090
And so to this day, even with all the gold
in Westeros to tempt invaders, Casterly Rock

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.060
has never fallen.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.039
At least not in battle.

00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:48.200
The castle is sadly all that remains of its
namesake family, the Casterlys.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:53.869
According to another legend, my ancestor Lann
the Clever, swindled the castle from them.

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:58.719
The most common story is that he found a hidden
cleft in the rock and snuck into the castle.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:02:04.299
As night, he whispered threats into sleeping
ears, howled in the darkness, planted one

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:07.450
brother's treasures in the room of another,
and so forth.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:13.930
By the end of his games, the Casterlys believed
a demon was haunting their home and fled.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.510
My brother prefers a different version.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:21.120
Lann the Clever did find a secret entrance
into the rock but used it to have his way

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.900
with the Casterly maidens.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:28.090
Eventually, the girls gave birth to golden-haired
bastards, and the Casterlys had no choice

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.390
but to accept their father into the family.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:38.569
In gratitude, he changed the family name to
honor himself, and House Lannister was born.

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:42.360
The Casterlys used the gold of the rock to
become lords.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.140
The Lannisters became kings.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.519
For thousands of years, the Kingdom of the
Rock ruled the Westerlands.

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:54.049
When the ironborn became a nuisance, my ancestor
sailed to the Iron Islands and returned with

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:59.430
a hundred ironborn hostages, promising to
hang one from the rock every time the ironborn

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.540
dared raid our shores.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.860
The ironborn stayed away, well, after twenty
or so.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.019
When the Andals arrived after sweeping across
the rest of Westeros, we invited their sons

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:13.120
and daughters into the rock as squires and
court ladies.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.159
I don't think we ever had to hang any of them.

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:23.180
Finally, Aegon the Conqueror defeated us on
the Field of Fire, and my ancestor knelt.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:29.690
Still, little changed but titles and taxes,
for when Visenya Targaryen saw the rock, she

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.480
gave thanks that my ancestor had met Aegon
on the field.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.409
Even dragon flame would have washed over the
castle like the waves and left just as much

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:38.409
a mark.

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.519
Jaime Lannister: When disciplining unruly
vassals, most lords send armies.

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:46.879
My father, Tywin, only had to send a singer.

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:54.099
There's no faster way to dull a vassal's ambition
or any festive occasion than hearing The Rains

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:56.120
of Castamere.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:01.959
House Reyne of Castamere was an old and proud
house that was slowly sinking back into the

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:02.959
muck.

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:03.959
Their mines had run dry.

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:07.620
Without gold, they turned to a more common
source of wealth.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.950
Daughters.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.780
Lady Ellyn Reyne was betrothed to my great
uncle.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:17.190
But when he fell in battle, Lady Ellyn sought
comfort in his twin brother's bed, beating

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.320
out the other woman he had promised to marry.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.630
Then the husband, who had shared his twin's
wife, shared his twin's death on a different

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:25.950
battlefield.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:32.530
Lady Ellyn flung herself at the new and married
heir to the Rock, but my grandfather Tytos

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.810
was more kitten than lion.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.970
He ran away and told his wife of Lady Ellyn's
designs, and Lady Ellyn soon found herself

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:45.190
married off to WalderanTarbeck, lord of another
failing house.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:50.310
The Reynes and Tarbecks should have sunk into
obscurity together, and they would have if

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.410
not for my grandfather becoming Lord of Casterly
Rock.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:59.510
At first, the Westerlands laughed with the
"Laughing Lion," as the jovial Tytos was called.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:05.510
But when men realized this lion had neither
teeth nor claws, they started to laugh at

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.700
him.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.330
None laughed harder than the Reynes and Tarbecks.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:15.230
Though Lady Ellyn was no longer welcome at
Casterly Rock, Tytos didn't refuse her brothers

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:21.480
Roger and Reynard Reyne, not even when they
asked for extravagant loans.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.890
Thanks to our family's gold, Lady Ellyn restored
Tarbeck Hall to a splendor she hadn't known

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.460
since being cast out of our home.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:35.900
When my grandfather broached the subject of
repayment, Roger and Reynard only laughed.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.650
And soon enough, my grandfather was laughing
along with them.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:44.110
Then my father Tywin returned from the War
of the Ninepenny Kings, where he'd seen how

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.110
the rest of the realm sniggered at House Lannister.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:52.590
Determined to restore our proper place, my
father demanded the immediate repayment of

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:57.750
all debts to the Rock or a hostage from those
who couldn't pay.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:01.750
Reynard Reyne merely laughed when he received
the raven.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:07.150
Lord WalderanTarbeck chose to ride to Casterly
Rock, sure that he could cow Lord Tytos into

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.910
rescinding my father's commands.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:15.570
He could have, except it wasn't Tytos who
met him at the gates but my father, who had

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.110
Lord Walderan thrown into a dungeon.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.830
Lady Ellyn protested.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.660
The Reynes threatened war.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:26.460
And finally, my grandfather broke and released
Lord Tarbeck with an apology, no less.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:33.780
As if bathing himself in shame, Tytos further
forgave all the Tarbeck debts to our house.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:39.050
To celebrate the end of hostilities, Lord
Roger feasted Tytos at Castamere, and the

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:43.060
two lords proclaimed their friendship for
eternity.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.980
My father allowed eternity to last a year.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.160
When he summoned the Reynes and Tarbecks to
Casterly Rock to answer for their crimes,

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.600
they rose in revolt, exactly as he expected.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.420
Their defiance gave him a pretext to call
his banners and ride for Tarbeck Hall and

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.750
Castamere with an army behind him.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.780
He didn't even bother to inform my grandfather.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:10.430
My father's army descended on the Tarbecks
so quickly that Lord Walderan had no time

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:15.910
to gather his forces, and rode against my
father with only his household knights.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.960
Soon his head, his sons' heads, and the heads
of any man with Tarbeck blood adorned the

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.120
spears of the Lannister vanguard as it marched
to Tarbeck Hall.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:31.330
At their approach, Lady Ellyn Tarbeck closed
the gates and sent ravens to her brothers

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.920
at Castamere.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:36.520
She assumed they'd have more than enough time
to muster their armies and break what would

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.610
be a long siege.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:46.810
My father had trebuchets up in a day and brought
down the keep within hours.

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:49.650
Lady Ellyn and her son were crushed in its
fall.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:56.080
When the Tarbeck forces surrendered, my father
put their castle to the torch.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.240
Roger Reyne arrived with his army just in
time to see the flames consuming his sister's

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.240
home.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:06.700
He charged my father's camp, hoping surprise
would win out over my father's great numbers.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:08.110
It didn't.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:13.900
With half his men dead on the field and a
cross-bolt in his back, Lord Roger fled back

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.200
to Castamere.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.300
The Lannister host arrived at Castamere three
days later.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.090
Like Casterly Rock, the seat of House Reyne
had begun as a mine.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:28.300
When the gold gave out, the mine shafts were
widened into halls, galleries, and bedchambers

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.400
deep beneath the earth.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.440
The Reyne brothers didn't have the men to
defend the castle walls and retreated into

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.760
their underground stronghold.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:42.820
From this relative safety, they offered terms
to my father to avoid a long siege.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.480
My father didn't reply.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.010
Instead, he commanded that the mines be sealed
with stone and soil until there was no way

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.140
in and no way out.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.630
When that was completed, it took less than
a day to dam the stream beside the castle

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:59.960
and only two to divert it to the nearest mine
entrance.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:06.320
The Reynes had taken more than three hundred
men, women, and children into the mines.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:11.010
A few guards reported hearing faint screams
and shouts below them one night.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:16.870
But come dawn, the earth was silent once again.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:23.710
And now the rain weeps o'er their halls, with
no one left to hear.

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:29.410
Tywin Lannister: On the far western coast
of the continent, high atop a rocky promontory

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:37.230
overlooking the Sunset Sea, sits Casterly
Rock, ancestral seat of House Lannister.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:40.750
Below it lies Lannisport, one of the great
cities of Westeros.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:46.780
A center of trade, culture, and the great
Lannister fleet.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:51.340
There are a number of gold and silver mines
in the Westerlands, making it the richest

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.140
region in all of Westeros.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:59.020
One of our most productive gold mines lies
beneath Casterly Rock itself, making House

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:03.290
Lannister the wealthiest of all the noble
houses.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.690
This allows House Lannister to fund many endeavors
of other noble houses.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:13.480
Even the king himself has sought credit from
Casterly Rock from time to time.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:20.250
We Lannisters claim our descent from the Andal
invaders and, through the female bloodline,

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.940
Lann the Clever.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:27.310
According to the legend, Lann, using only
his wits, won Casterly Rock from the noble

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:30.330
house of Casterly during the Age of Heroes.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:36.280
The Lannisters reigned as Kings of the Rock
for thousands of years and worked to make

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.510
it the envy of the rest of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:47.150
Our time as kings ended, however, when Aegon
Targaryen, otherwise known as Aegon the Conqueror,

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:50.380
arrived in Westeros with his army.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:56.300
The last King of the Rock, King Loren Lannister,
joined forces with King Mern Gardener, the

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.460
King of the Reach.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:04.510
Together, with sixty thousand men, they met
the Targaryen host in open battle.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:10.820
History tells us that Aegon unleashed all
three of his dragons, slaughtering four thousand

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:16.000
men at what came to be known as "the Field
of Fire."

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:23.360
King Mern himself was burned alive that day,
and House Gardener turned to ash with him.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:31.660
Seeing both the threat and opportunity the
Targaryens represented, Loren wisely surrendered

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:36.320
and aided Aegon in his further conquest of
Westeros.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:43.870
The Lannisters were thus appointed Lords Paramount
of the Westerlands and Wardens of the West,

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:47.690
titles we hold to this day.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.780
Let us be clear.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:55.650
It is neither luck nor royal favor that makes
our House prosperous.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:01.210
There have been times in our history when
some have considered thought us weak, lazy,

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:02.850
or opulent.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:09.280
My father, Tytos Lannister, nearly bankrupted
our House with his poor investments and allowed

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.980
himself to be mocked openly at court.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:18.350
When our vassal, the Reynes of Castamere,
dared to rise against the Lannisters, they

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:22.050
learned how dangerous it can be to taunt a
lion.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:27.540
I, Tywin Lannister, personally led the assault
on Castamere to put down this rebellion.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:33.920
I made an example of them, to anyone who doubts
our might.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.770
They even made a quaint song about the fate
of the Reynes of Castamere.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:42.450
But sadly, there are no Reynes left to hear
it.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:49.350
Today the golden Lion of Lannister is rightly
admired and feared throughout the Seven Kingdoms.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:57.770
Our words are "Hear me Roar," but there are
of other words that should be remembered when

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.630
crossing a lion of Casterly Rock.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:04.200
"A Lannister always pays his debts."

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:08.870
As I said, for free you can now listen to
the entire audiobook Fire &amp; Blood, on which

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:14.100
House of the Dragon is based and which covers
the entire Targaryen history, including current

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:19.030
and future events of House of the Dragon,
for free with an audible trial using our link

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.790
in the description.

